 mention any of [&#x27;primary insomnia&#x27;, &#x27;insomnia&#x27;, &#x27;sleep onset latency&#x27;, &#x27;sleep latency&#x27;] (an incidental abstract mention does not qualify).</td><td class='span'>examined title/conditions: “Total Joint Arthroplasty and Sleep Primary Total Hip Arthroplasty Primary Total Knee Arthr…”</td></tr><tr><td>NCT06996171</td><td>nct</td><td class='dec-exclude'>exclude</td><td>X3</td><td>UNRECORDED</td><td>intervention is the wrong form: matches excluded &#x27;magnesium&#x27; (receptor agonist/analogue, combination, or measured-not-randomised).</td><td class='span'>Comparative Efficacy of Magnesium Supplement and Melatoni…</td></tr><tr><td>NCT02087722</td><td>nct</td><td class='dec-exclude'>exclude</td><td>X3</td><td>UNRECORDED</td><td>the randomised intervention is not [&#x27;melatonin&#x27;, &#x27;prolonged-release melatonin&#x27;, &#x27;controlled-release melatonin&#x27;, &#x27;circadin&#x27;] (not named in title/conditions; an incidental abstract mention does not qualify).</td><td class='span'>examined: “Efficacy and Safety of KI1001 in the Treatment of ≥ 55 Years Old Insomnia Patients Sleep I…”</td></tr><tr><td>NCT01489969</td><td>nct</td><td class='dec-exclude'>exclude</td><td>X3</td><td>UNRECORDED</td><td>the randomised intervention is not [&#x27;melatonin&#x27;, &#x27;prolonged-release melatonin&#x27;, &#x27;controlled-release melatonin&#x27;, &#x27;circadin&#x27;] (not named in title/conditions; an incidental abstract mention does not qualify).</td><td class='span'>examined: “Sleep Laboratory Study to Investigate the Safety and Efficacy of Neu-P11 in Primary Insomn…”</td></tr><tr><td>MelatoZincME · NCT05454683</td><td>nct</td><td class='dec-exclude'>exclude</td><td>X2</td><td>UNRECORDED</td><td>population not on-topic: title/conditions do not mention any of [&#x27;primary insomnia&#x27;, &#x27;insomnia&#x27;, &#x27;sleep onset latency&#x27;, &#x27;sleep latency&#x27;] (an incidental abstract mention does not qualify).</td><td class='span'>examined title/conditions: “Melatonin and Zinc Administration on Cardinal Symptoms in Myalgic Encephalomyelitis/Chroni…”</td></tr><tr><td>NCT01450228</td><td>nct</td><td class='dec-exclude'>exclude</td><td>X3</td><td>UNRECORDED</td><td>the randomised intervention is not [&#x27;melatonin&#x27;, &#x27;prolonged-release melatonin&#x27;, &#x27;controlled-release melatonin&#x27;, &#x27;circadin&#x27;] (not named in title/conditions; an incidental abstract mention does not qualify).</td><td class='span'>examined: “Efficacy and Safety of KI1001 in ≥ 55 Years Old Insomnia Patients Sleep Initiation and Mai…”</td></tr><tr><td>Neu I · NCT00816673</td><td>nct</td><td class='dec-include'>include</td><td>INCLUDE</td><td>UNRECORDED</td><td>eligible double-blind/placebo-controlled RCT: intervention circadin, comparator placebo, population primary insomnia — P/I/C/design met.</td><td class='span'>population “…n In Elderly Insomniacs Primary Insomnia Neu I”; comparator “…mniacs Primary Insomnia placebo Circadin Circadin Neu I”</td></tr></table><h4>Controls</h4><ul><li><strong>Positive:</strong> Recovered &amp; included the canonical trials [&#x27;20712869&#x27;] that a comparator includes; none missed.</li><li><strong>Negative:</strong> Cross-topic trial(s) [&#x27;25862116&#x27;] recovered by the search and correctly EXCLUDED [&#x27;25862116&#x27;] by rule (same drug/design, wrong topic).</li></ul></section><section class="tab" id="tab-outcomes"><h3 class="tabname">Results</h3><div class='absent'><strong>Cross-family definition audit.</strong> Two independent model families (Gemini via AGY, and Fable) re-read every pooled row and checked whether the extracted result matches the outcome LABEL's definition &mdash; composite component set, timepoint, population, analysis set &mdash; not just the number. Rows flagged for this topic, with how each was resolved (refuse the trial / disclose the heterogeneity / relabel the timepoint / already disclosed). This is the endpoint-<strong>IDENTITY</strong> check &mdash; distinct from the per-number <strong>MAGNITUDE</strong> check (every pooled number located in its committed source span, gate-enforced). A number can pass magnitude and fail identity, which is exactly the class this audit catches; &lsquo;verified&rsquo; on this harness now means both:<table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Outcome</th><th>Finding</th><th>Resolution</th></tr><tr><td>20712869</td><td>Sleep-onset latency</td><td>Age 65-80 subgroup of an 18-80 enrolment.</td><td><strong>ALREADY DISCLOSED (population field states the subgroup)</strong></td></tr></table></div><h4>Sleep-onset latency (primary)</h4><table class='kv'><tr><th>Estimand</th><td>MD</td></tr><tr><th>Analysis population</th><td>pre-specified age 65-80 ITT subgroup (of an 18-80 enrolment)</td></tr><tr><th>Timepoint</th><td>end of treatment</td></tr><tr><th>Method</th><td>Single included trial that reported this outcome — the estimate is that trial&#x27;s own effect; no random-effects pooling (tau^2, HKSJ and prediction interval are not applicable at k=1).</td></tr><tr><th>k</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Single-trial effect</th><td>-17.4 (MD), 95% CI -28.52–-6.28</td></tr><tr><th>Note</th><td>prediction interval undefined for k=1</td></tr><tr><th>Leave-one-out (influence)</th><td>not assessable at k=1 (leave-one-out needs k&amp;gt;=3)</td></tr></table><h5>Compatibility key (pooling contract)</h5><table class='kv'><tr><th>Effect-measure class</th><td>CONTINUOUS</td></tr><tr><th>Effect-measure labels pooled</th><td></td></tr><tr><th>Endpoint</th><td>single endpoint</td></tr><tr><th>Follow-up window</th><td>end of treatment</td></tr><tr><th>Analysis set</th><td>pre-specified age 65-80 ITT subgroup (of an 18-80 enrolment)</td></tr><tr><th>Randomised contrast (registry-confirmed)</th><td>1 of 1 pooled trials</td></tr></table><p class='note'>k = 1: the 1 trial(s) named below were pooled; 8 further screened-in trial(s) had no poolable value for this outcome and are listed below with an explicit <em>absence state</em>. These are four different things and only one is a claim about the trial: <em>no outcome data in source</em> (the full text was retrieved and is silent — the only state that means the trial itself lacks the outcome; 3 here) vs. <em>not extracted</em> (the number IS in the retrieved source — an extraction gap, about us, not the trial), <em>abstract only, full text not retrieved</em> (absence in the trial is unproven), and <em>excluded on evidence</em> (a number was found and deliberately not pooled — see reason). An unassessed outcome never counts as favourable to the intervention.</p><table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Id</th><th>Input</th><th>Source</th></tr><tr><td>20712869</td><td>PMID 20712869</td><td>-19.1±47.3 (n=137) vs -1.7±47.8 (n=144) (mean±SD) <span class='muted' title='effect computed by the harness from arm-level data, not the trial-reported effect'>· harness-reconstructed</span></td><td><span class='vok' title='continuous per-arm mean/SD present in committed source'>✓ verified against source</span><br>ClinicalTrials.gov results (structured, continuous): outcome &#x27;The Change From Baseline in Subjective Sleep Latency.&#x27; mean -19.1 (SD 47.3, n=137) [Circadin] vs -1.7 (SD 47.8, n=144) [Placebo] minutes — population: Pre-planned analysis on ITT population age 65-80<div class='ident'><em>design key:</em> UNKNOWN / unit UNKNOWN; estimator RECONSTRUCTED; correlation handling none; action ALLOW_WITH_LABEL</div></td></tr><tr><td>33157425</td><td>PMID 33157425</td><td class='absent-cell'>not established — abstract only; full text not retrieved, so absence in the trial is unproven</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>22346363</td><td>PMID 22346363</td><td class='absent-cell'>declared absent — no outcome data in the retrieved source</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>27559258</td><td>PMID 27559258</td><td class='absent-cell'>declared absent — no outcome data in the retrieved source</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>19584739</td><td>PMID 19584739</td><td class='absent-cell'>not established — abstract only; full text not retrieved, so absence in the trial is unproven</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>18036082</td><td>PMID 18036082</td><td class='absent-cell'>not established — abstract only; full text not retrieved, so absence in the trial is unproven</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>17875243</td><td>PMID 17875243</td><td class='absent-cell'>not established — abstract only; full text not retrieved, so absence in the trial is unproven</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>12790159</td><td>PMID 12790159</td><td class='absent-cell'>declared absent — no outcome data in the retrieved source</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>Neu I</td><td>NCT00816673</td><td class='absent-cell'>not established — abstract only; full text not retrieved, so absence in the trial is unproven</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr></table></section><section class="tab" id="tab-harms"><h3 class="tabname">Harms</h3><h4>Adverse events</h4><div class="absent"><strong>DECLARED ABSENT.</strong> REPORTED but not extractable as a pooled value: 33157425, 22346363, 20712869, 18036082, 12790159 mention this outcome in the committed abstract, but without arm counts or an effect+CI in an extractable form (e.g. a bare percentage with no denominator). This outcome is NOT absent — it is reported-but-not-poolable from the committed source; full-text acquisition would recover the countable form.</div><table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Id</th><th>Input</th><th>Source</th></tr><tr><td>33157425</td><td>PMID 33157425</td><td class='absent-cell'>not established — abstract only; full text not retrieved, so absence in the trial is unproven</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>22346363</td><td>PMID 22346363</td><td class='absent-cell'>declared absent — no outcome data in the retrieved source</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>27559258</td><td>PMID 27559258</td><td class='absent-cell'>declared absent — no outcome data in the retrieved source</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>20712869</td><td>PMID 20712869</td><td class='absent-cell'>declared absent — no outcome data in the retrieved source</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>19584739</td><td>PMID 19584739</td><td class='absent-cell'>not established — abstract only; full text not retrieved, so absence in the trial is unproven</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>18036082</td><td>PMID 18036082</td><td class='absent-cell'>not established — abstract only; full text not retrieved, so absence in the trial is unproven</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>17875243</td><td>PMID 17875243</td><td class='absent-cell'>not established — abstract only; full text not retrieved, so absence in the trial is unproven</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>12790159</td><td>PMID 12790159</td><td class='absent-cell'>not extracted — the outcome&#x27;s number IS in the source (extraction gap, not trial absence)</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr><tr><td>Neu I</td><td>NCT00816673</td><td class='absent-cell'>not established — abstract only; full text not retrieved, so absence in the trial is unproven</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract</td></tr></table></section><section class="tab" id="tab-comparator"><h3 class="tabname">Comparator</h3><table class='kv'><tr><th>Published comparator</th><td>Meta-analysis: melatonin for the treatment of primary sleep disorders. (2013), PLoS One</td></tr><tr><th>Identifier</th><td>PMID 23691095</td></tr><tr><th>Open access</th><td>True</td></tr><tr><th>URL</th><td>https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0063773</td></tr></table><h4>Scope match (is this the same question?)</h4><p><strong>✓ same question.</strong> Intervention level: topic is a single agent, comparator is a single agent (match: True); population match: True. same-question comparator (matching intervention level and population) <span class='muted'>Decided by one uniform rule applied to every topic before the k was seen.</span></p><h4>Trial-set overlap (an identical estimate on an identical set is arithmetic, not corroboration)</h4><table class='kv'><tr><th>k in this review (our own search)</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>k stated in the comparator&#x27;s own text (auto-extracted)</th><td>not stated in the comparator abstract/full text</td></tr><tr><th>Shared trials</th><td>not exactly verifiable (comparator trial table not machine-exposed)</td></tr><tr><th>Only in ours</th><td>33157425, 27559258</td></tr><tr><th>Only in theirs</th><td></td></tr><tr><th>Overlap method</th><td>publication-date + design identity (comparator trial list not extracted from source)</td></tr><tr><th>Note</th><td>Trials newer than the comparator (2013) cannot be in it (only-ours, verifiable by date). Exact shared count not asserted.</td></tr></table><p class='note'>The comparator <em>k</em> above is auto-extracted from the comparator's own text and may reference a sub-analysis rather than its same-scope pooled total; the <strong>enumerated same-scope comparator <em>k</em></strong> (scope-classified, the finishing metric) is the figure in the parity table, which governs where these differ.</p></section><section class="tab" id="tab-riskofbias"><h3 class="tabname">Risk of bias</h3><p><strong>Coverage: 1 of 1 primary-outcome pooled trials assessed</strong> (1 from registry (AACT) + trial text)</p><div class='banner'><strong>RoB spans span-checked (cross-family): 97% agreement</strong> (32 of 33 scoreable), from a seeded sample of 45 model/registry-derived domain ratings independently checked by a different model family (Fable) against each trial abstract; 12 were unscoreable (no claim, or a conservative not-stated rating). This check itself found and fixed a real error &mdash; one trial (EMPHASIS-HF) was mislabelled NON_RANDOMIZED by the registry, contradicted by its abstract; the RoB block was also visibly broken until a human review caught it. The number is here because a RoB block a reader cannot trust is worthless (<code>docs/rob_spancheck.json</code>).</div><div class='absent'><strong>Randomised-contrast disclosure (per pooled trial, from the registry arm structure — disclosed, not an adjustment).</strong> Eligibility should test what actually DIFFERS between the randomised arms, not the mere presence of the drug word: a trial giving the drug of interest as BACKGROUND in every arm (e.g. all arms on the same agent, randomising a different drug) is not a randomised comparison of it. For each pooled trial the randomised contrast is reconstructed from AACT <code>design_groups</code> + <code>interventions</code>: <strong>1 of 1</strong> pooled trials have a registry-confirmed contrast (the intervention of interest differs across arms). A trial with no registry arm data, or coded under a class label / development code we cannot machine-match, is shown as <em>contrast unverified</em> — a VISIBLE fail-open state, never silently treated as verified. <table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Contrast status</th><th>Randomised difference</th></tr><tr><td>20712869</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>circadin</td></tr></table></div><div class='absent'><strong>Funding / conflict-of-interest disclosure (per pooled trial, from source — disclosed, not adjusted).</strong> Industry-funded trials are a documented reporting-bias dimension (they tend to report more favourable results). For each pooled trial the funding source is classified from a verbatim statement in the committed source (full text preferred, abstract fallback), including an industry <em>drug-supply</em> tie in an otherwise independently funded trial: <strong>0 of 0 known</strong> (1 unknown) pooled trials are industry-funded or industry-tied (the industry-funded proportion of trials with KNOWN funding — unknown-funding trials are reported separately below, not counted as independently funded — for comparison against a comparator's). Absence is labelled by how deeply we looked — 0 with no funding statement in the <strong>full text</strong> (genuinely silent) and 1 where only the <strong>abstract</strong> was available (full text not retrieved) — so 'not stated' is never presented as 'independently funded'. The harness <strong>does not adjust</strong> for funding (the per-trial bias magnitude is not quantifiable from a funding line) — it is disclosed so a reader can weigh it. Never inferred.<table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Funding</th><th>Scanned</th><th>Verbatim statement</th></tr><tr><td>PMID 20712869</td><td>not stated (abstract only — full text not retrieved)</td><td>abstract only</td><td></td></tr></table></div><p><strong>Machine-derived risk-of-bias signals</strong> (per pooled trial) &mdash; NOT a formal Cochrane RoB2 assessment, which requires human judgements the registry cannot supply. These are computed from what is machine-available (AACT 2026-08-30 + registry-vs-pooled (D5)). <strong>Domain 5 (selective reporting)</strong> is computed from the trial's REGISTERED primary outcome vs the outcome we pooled — a machine-checkable signal most published meta-analyses do not report. D1/D2/D4 use AACT structured allocation/masking fields. <strong>D3 (missing outcome data) is NOT ASSESSED for any trial — a stated limitation, not a per-trial judgement</strong>: the harness has no outcome-missingness evidence source (study discontinuation is not outcome missingness), so D3 is structurally unassessable here and is never rated; the attrition figures are shown as context only. This caps overall GRADE certainty below <em>high</em> corpus-wide (a required bias domain is unassessed), and it would be fixed by a committed outcome-missingness source (AACT <code>milestones</code> / the publication's flow diagram: analysed-vs-randomised at the outcome). Other risk-of-bias judgements that need human reading are likewise marked <em>not assessed</em>: partial-but-honest, never guessed. Hover a cell for its basis.</p><table class='recs'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Overall</th><th>D1 randomisation</th><th>D2 deviations/blinding</th><th>D3 missing data</th><th>D4 measurement</th><th>D5 selective reporting</th></tr><tr><td>20712869</td><td><strong>low (on assessed domains; some domains require human judgement)</strong></td><td title='AACT allocation = RANDOMIZED'>low</td><td title='trial masking = Double (blinded); overrides per-role Booleans subject_masked=True/caregiver_masked=False (FLAGGED registry-vs-trial disagreement)'>low</td><td title='no AACT participant-flow data; outcome missingness needs human judgement'>not assessed</td><td title='trial masking = Double (blinded); overrides outcomes_assessor_masked=False (FLAGGED registry-vs-trial disagreement)'>low</td><td title='the pooled outcome IS the trial&#x27;s pre-registered primary outcome'>low</td></tr></table><h4>Risk-of-bias sensitivity (re-pooled with the same estimator)</h4><div class='absent'><strong>Does the result survive dropping the trials that are not low risk of bias?</strong> The primary outcome is re-pooled by risk-of-bias stratum with the identical estimator. <strong>1 of 1</strong> pooled trials have a risk-of-bias rating; no pooled trial is rated <em>high</em> risk (the registry-derived assessment does not reach 'high'), so the standard drop-high sensitivity is inert and the informative stratum is <em>low-only</em>. An unrated trial cannot be placed in a stratum, so a low-only pool with fewer trials than the full pool reflects both risk of bias and assessment coverage &mdash; read the widened interval with that caveat, not as instability of the effect.<table class='arms'><tr><th>Stratum</th><th>Re-pooled estimate</th></tr><tr><td>Full pool (all pooled trials)</td><td>k=1, MD -17.4 [-28.5214, -6.2786]</td></tr><tr><td>Low risk of bias only</td><td>k=1, MD -17.4 [-28.5214, -6.2786] <em>(fewer trials than the full pool &mdash; see coverage)</em></td></tr></table></div><h4>GRADE certainty (PROVISIONAL — partial, object-derived)</h4><div class='absent'><strong>Overall certainty (provisional): moderate</strong> (starting from <em>high</em> for randomized trials, 0 downgrade(s)).<strong>PROVISIONAL:</strong> this is a machine-derived certainty — risk of bias uses machine-derived signals (not a human RoB2) and indirectness is not auto-rated, so a formal human GRADE assessment may differ. Risk of bias, inconsistency, imprecision and publication bias are computed from committed fields; <strong>publication bias is assessed from the registry ghost census, not funnel-plot asymmetry</strong> (which is unreliable at our small k). <strong>Indirectness is left to human judgement</strong> (the PICO scope note states the directness) &mdash; this is a partial GRADE, honestly labelled.<table class='arms'><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Effect on certainty</th><th>Basis</th></tr><tr><td>Risk of bias</td><td>not downgraded</td><td>none of the 1 assessed trial(s) at high risk; fewer than half at &#x27;some concerns&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Inconsistency</td><td><strong>NOT ASSESSED</strong></td><td>single trial (k=1): between-study inconsistency is not estimable</td></tr><tr><td>Imprecision</td><td>not downgraded</td><td>95% CI [-28.5214, -6.2786]; single trial — imprecision judged from the CI, not downgraded merely for k=1</td></tr><tr><td>Indirectness</td><td>human judgement</td><td>directness of population/intervention/comparator/outcome is a human judgement; not auto-rated (the scope note on the page states the PICO)</td></tr><tr><td>Publication bias (registry-based)</td><td><strong>NOT ASSESSED</strong></td><td>no registry ghost census available for this topic</td></tr></table></div></section><section class="tab" id="tab-manuscript"><h3 class="tabname">Manuscript</h3><div class='banner'>This manuscript is <strong>generated from the review object</strong> — every number is interpolated from a committed field, and a gate limb refuses any manuscript numeral that is not object-derived. It is a machine artefact, not a hand-written paper.</div><h4>Abstract</h4><p><strong>Question.</strong> In adults with primary insomnia, does melatonin reduce sleep-onset latency versus placebo? (Randomized placebo-controlled trials; mean difference in minutes.)</p><p><strong>Methods.</strong> This review is NOT prospectively registered in this repository: the protocol first entered the repository inside a build commit (SHA 146edbf72435), so precedence of protocol over synthesis is not demonstrated here. The registry-first (AACT) adapter did NOT complete for this topic (status RAN_ERROR); the evidence set was assembled by known-item retrieval, NOT a completed registry-first or systematic search (retracted claim)